  "2026-07-27T21:05:14.401Z","harness:codex","Dedupe evidence: all-status search for MCP custom-field collision diagnostics reviewed the canonical reserved-field fix pm-b9ov, runtime projection pm-m4ikkz, and exact collision guard pm-xwah; none owns author-facing MCP transport/tool-input diagnostics. CodeRabbit final review raised this distinct low-noise UX follow-up."
  "2026-08-03T07:39:30.736Z","harness:codex","TDD evidence: schema add-field, profile lint, and extension doctor tests now cover canonical MCP ownership collisions and options.<field> recovery. Dispatch remains unchanged; the diagnostic is author-time and deterministic."
  "2026-08-03T08:06:46.625Z","harness:codex","Evidence: repo-wide static quality now passes with 100% module/export/member docstrings, zero clone findings, public SDK boundary closure, token/context gates, SDK entrypoint cost checks, and CLI transport floor. Collision diagnostics were split into a focused SDK module instead of raising the 3,400-line architecture budget."
  "2026-08-03T08:23:08.556Z","harness:codex","Manual acceptance: schema add-field cwd emitted custom_field_mcp_input_collision:cwd:cwd:mcp_tool_input:use=options.cwd in a fresh workspace. The packed SDK resolver maps pm-executable to options.pmExecutable without changing dispatch."
